      "sec": "NEO product Info page, printed to PDF 2026-04-08",
      "src": 96,
      "url": "https://www.1enrollment.com/information/product.cfm?page=39509&id=767303",
      "v": "Footnotes shared across all three Allstate STM PPO plans: 'Out-of-network deductibles and coinsurances are DOUBLE their in-network amounts. Coinsurance percentages are the same for out-of-network services.' 'The family deductible is capped at 3x the individual deductible. For families with more than 3 members, all covered expenses accumulate towards the family deductible, but no individual member will pay more than their individual deductible. Additional copays apply to deductible and coinsurance.' 'Copays are not applicable to out-of-network services. NO WAITING PERIOD APPLIES. Includes services such as Surgeon, Anesthesia, Office Visits, Preventive Services, Urgent Care, Diagnostics and Lab. A $5,000 BENEFIT LIMIT APPLIES TO OUTPATIENT TREATMENT OF A JOINT, NECK, SPINE, OR CONNECTIVE TISSUE including tendons, ligaments, and cartilage (exclusions may apply, see exclusion list). There is also a 30 VISIT LIMIT FOR PT, OT, ST Cardiac and Pulmonary rehabilitation.' Common benefit treatment: office visits including preventive, adult screenings, inpatient services and diagnostic/x-ray/lab all apply to deductible and coinsurance; emergency room applies to deductible and coinsurance with a $250 ACCESS FEE WAIVED IF ADMITTED; urgent care carries a $50 ACCESS FEE with the deductible waived and the remainder subject to coinsurance; child immunizations are a FIRST DOLLAR BENEFIT.",
      "vs": "VERIFIED_SINGLE_SOURCE"
    },
